# Redis Rate Limiting Configuration Example
# Copy relevant settings to your .env file

# ============================================================================
# OPTION 1: Redis URL (Recommended - Single connection string)
# ============================================================================

# Production (Upstash, Redis Cloud, etc. - with TLS)
# REDIS_URL=rediss://default:YOUR_PASSWORD@YOUR_HOST:6379

# Development (Local Redis - without TLS)
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# ============================================================================
# OPTION 2: Individual Redis Settings (Alternative)
# ============================================================================

# Redis Host
# REDIS_HOST=localhost

# Redis Port
# REDIS_PORT=6379

# Redis Password (leave empty for local development)
# REDIS_PASSWORD=

# Redis Database Number (0-15)
# REDIS_DB=0

# Redis SSL/TLS (true for production, false for local)
# REDIS_SSL=false

# ============================================================================
# Rate Limiting Control
# ============================================================================

# Enable/Disable Redis-based rate limiting
# Set to false to disable rate limiting entirely (development only)
REDIS_ENABLED=true

# ============================================================================
# Rate Limit Configuration (Already set in config.py)
# ============================================================================
# These are already configured with sensible defaults.
# Override only if you need custom limits.

# RATE_LIMIT_FREE=10          # Free tier: 10 requests/minute
# RATE_LIMIT_STARTER=60       # Starter tier: 60 requests/minute
# RATE_LIMIT_PRO=120          # Pro tier: 120 requests/minute
# RATE_LIMIT_ENTERPRISE=300   # Enterprise tier: 300 requests/minute

# ============================================================================
# Quick Start Examples
# ============================================================================

# Example 1: Local Redis for Development
# ----------------------------------------
# 1. Install Redis: brew install redis (macOS) or apt install redis-server (Ubuntu)
# 2. Start Redis: brew services start redis (macOS) or sudo systemctl start redis (Ubuntu)
# 3. Add to .env:
#    REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
#    REDIS_ENABLED=true

# Example 2: Upstash (Serverless Redis)
# ----------------------------------------
# 1. Create free account at https://upstash.com
# 2. Create a Redis database
# 3. Copy the connection URL from dashboard
# 4. Add to .env:
#    REDIS_URL=rediss://default:YOUR_PASSWORD@YOUR_HOST:6379
#    REDIS_ENABLED=true

# Example 3: Redis Cloud
# ----------------------------------------
# 1. Create free account at https://redis.com/try-free/
# 2. Create a database
# 3. Get connection details from dashboard
# 4. Add to .env:
#    REDIS_URL=rediss://default:YOUR_PASSWORD@YOUR_HOST:PORT
#    REDIS_ENABLED=true

# Example 4: Docker Redis (Development)
# ----------------------------------------
# 1. Run: docker run -d -p 6379:6379 --name redis redis:7-alpine
# 2. Add to .env:
#    REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
#    REDIS_ENABLED=true

# ============================================================================
# Troubleshooting
# ============================================================================

# Redis not connecting?
# - Check if Redis is running: redis-cli ping
# - Verify REDIS_URL format: redis:// (no TLS) or rediss:// (with TLS)
# - Check firewall rules for port 6379
# - Review logs for connection errors

# Rate limiting not working?
# - Verify REDIS_ENABLED=true in .env
# - Check rate limit headers in API responses (X-RateLimit-Limit, X-RateLimit-Remaining)
# - Test with: curl -i http://localhost:8000/health
# - Review API logs for Redis connection status

# Getting 429 Too Many Requests?
# - This means rate limiting is working correctly!
# - Wait for the reset time (check X-RateLimit-Reset header)
# - Upgrade your tier for higher limits
# - Or wait ~60 seconds for the window to reset
